// STATUS: ok
// float() gives the nearest Number to the decimal that its String names, so a
// String at or above the midpoint between the largest finite double and
// 2^1024 is an infinity and one at or below half the smallest subnormal is
// zero. The sign of the String applies to that result, so the negative cases
// give a negative infinity and a negative zero (spec/05-stdlib.md, float).

print float("");
// CHECK: inf

print float("-");
// CHECK: -inf

print float("0.");
// CHECK: 5e-324

print float("-0.");
// CHECK: -5e-324

print float("0.");
// CHECK: 0

print 1 / float("-0.");
// CHECK: -inf
